In larger instance sizes, even if trained with $N=20$, the NI model is not only able to maintain the good performance, but also improves the percentile rank of the selected action. It selects, on average, the $13^{rd}$ best action out of $2401$ for $N=50$ and the $32^{nd}$ out of $9801$ for $N=100$.


