\caption{
The object-specific appearance decoder architecture. 
The features in the quantized features maps $\mathbf{Q}$ are reduced by a subspace restriction module into non-quantized features $\tilde{\mathbf{F}}$ that are then vector-quantized (VQ) by the codebooks $\mathbf{K}$ into $\tilde{\mathbf{Q}}$, which are then decoded into an anomaly-free image $\mathbf{I}_{spc}$.
}
\label{fig:reconstructive}
\end{figure}

